abstract: >-
  The Agent Execution Integrity Benchmark (AEIB) Enterprise v1.0 is an
  offline-reproducible evaluation distribution demonstrating that autonomous AI
  agents suffer duplicate mutations when encountering semantic drift during retry
  loops following post-commit HTTP 504 transport severance. AEIB implements an
  in-process wire trap, causal lineage binding, authoritative PostgreSQL state
  probing with statement timeouts, deterministic disposition mapping, and
  offline-verifiable cryptographic receipts. This review candidate packages the
  verified v0.2.4 core (0/500 duplicate mutations, Rule-of-Three 95% upper bound
  of 0.60%) alongside Phase 2 enterprise extensions (MCP stdio proxy, telemetry,
  Grafana dashboard, and long-haul soak daemon). Status: review distribution;
  six gaps addressed by prototype controls and local tests; production-scale
  validation remains pending.
keywords:
  - agent governance
  - transport fault reconciliation
  - idempotency
  - AI safety
  - execution integrity
  - post-dispatch failure
  - local_harness
  - SQLite
  - PostgreSQL
  - deterministic testing
  - Rule of Three
  - MCP
